# Conquest Tinkerer — project rules

- Python ≥ 3.10, standard library first. Third-party imports only for live
  sponsor calls, always behind a `SAMPLE_MODE` fallback.
- Every sponsor call must degrade gracefully: no exception may abort a run.
- The product is the **Conquest Designer** (informal-economy worker agent:
  R10,000, R83/month for 36 months, buys itself back in year 3). Business type is
  self-declared free text and is **never** a gate or a validated category.
- The coupon is swept as **gross revenue − COGS**. That is the only financial
  check. Do not add microscopic underwriting of the underlying business.
- No money moves. The `gated_intent` ledger is record-only; status is `gated`,
  `rejected` or `escalated`, never `settled`.
- Acquisition copy MUST NOT promise the coupon and MUST NOT use speculative terms
  (guaranteed, risk-free, get rich, ...). It MUST include the risk disclosure.
  The Fidelity & Conflict Critic's deterministic rule layer is authoritative.
- A market whose sweep cannot back the coupon (or that has no live instrument)
  must be **escalated**, never sold.
- Bound every loop (revision budget, batch depth). No unbounded debates.
- Keep the repository light; sample data stays under a few KB.
- Never commit `.env` or API keys.
